  "question": {
    "text": "The internal energy of air in $4 \\mathrm{~m} \\times 4 \\mathrm{~m} \\times 3 \\mathrm{~m}$ sized room at 1 atmospheric pressure will be _______ $\\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~J}$. (Consider air as diatomic molecule)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "To find the internal energy of gas in the room.<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\mathrm{U}=\\mathrm{nC}_{\\mathrm{v}} \\mathrm{~T}=\\mathrm{n} \\frac{5 \\mathrm{RT}}{2} \\\\\n& =\\frac{5}{2} \\mathrm{PV}=\\frac{5}{2} \\times 10^5 \\times 48=12 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~J}<br/>\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
